1. What tools do you currently use for group work?
Currently I use Microsoft Word, Excel and PowerPoint, and sometimes github for my group assignments.

2. How do you usually communicate with your group members?
Typical communication is through teams. However, a more accessible uh communication method can easily be through messages, WhatsApp or Instagram.  Um, I prefer messages, but then for easy accessibility for some group members, WhatsApp may be the more preferred option. 


3. What difficulties do you face when working in a group?
The main difficulty is making sure everyone in the group is keeping up with their work and ensuring the overall group progress is proceeding as expected, but other than that, as long as communication is maintained well enough, most challenges should be overcomeable. 


4. Can you describe a situation where group work did not go well?
Well, there was a situation where during one of my group projects, since there was a big group and there were a lot of tasks that needed to be distributed, but the tasks were not clearly distributed as to who was doing which part. Uh a difficulty was that one half of the group project was getting completed uh with a lot of progress, but the remaining report was left aside until I had to step up and allocate tasks for each team member to ensure every part of the project was completed and accounted for.

5. How are tasks assigned in your group? Is this effective?
Typically when tasks, when we are notified of each task, we break them down into different sections such as uh, if it was for engineering, you would have a mechanical system, electrical system, etcera. Uh, it would firstly be distributed based off each person's strengths and their likings. If there are no particular likings or strengths, it will then be distributed evenly across the group. By evenly I mean regarding the size of each task. If it has been determined that the task um requires more time, it may be distributed to two people, instead of one person and is typically just determined by the size of the task and the estimated time of completion required. 


6. Have you experienced communication issues? How did they affect your work?
No, not really. I have been really lucky with all my groups so far. However, I have experienced some issues regarding the communication of quality and standards of project work. Um like during a big group report, as it was a um rather large-sized report, um each person was allocated different sections. However, um there was some sections that were not complete to the best standard or quality, so I had to recheck and ensure there was no errors including any grammatical and structural errors within the report. This meant that I was doing a bit more work then I expected. 


7. What features would improve your group work experience?
Features that would improve my group work experience would be to have a timetable or like a open shared timetable that can be used to track everyone's progress, as well as know each person's availability so that we could um plan a regular group meeting time for each week and maintain consistent group meetings and checkups throughout the semester. And making sure that everyone in the team is able to like meet up and discuss the tasks. 
